PROBLEM:
Given the names and grades for each student in a class of N students, store them in a nested list and print the name(s) of any student(s) having the second lowest grade.

Note: If there are multiple students with the second lowest grade, order their names alphabetically and print each name on a new line.

SOLUTION:
def solve_problem(students):
    scores = []
    needed_names = []
    for student in students:
        scores.append(student[1])
    updated_score = sorted(set(scores))
    # print(updated_score)
    second_lowest_score = updated_score[1]
    # print(second_lowest_score)
    
    for student in students:
        if student[1]==second_lowest_score:
            needed_names.append(student[0])
    # print(needed_names)
    for i in sorted(needed_names):
        print(i)
    
    
    
    

if __name__ == '__main__':
    students = []
    for _ in range(int(input())):
        name = input()
        score = float(input())
        students.append([name, score])
    solve_problem(students)
    

    
